Here is a simple example of how you can create a Rust app that supports the ElevenLabs.io API and reads the contents of the clipboard aloud using TTS:

First, add the following dependencies to your `Cargo.toml` file:
```toml
[dependencies]
elevenlabs = "0.1.0"
tts = "0.1.0"
clipboard = "0.1.0"
```
Then, create a new Rust file (e.g. `main.rs`) and add the following code:
```rust
use elevenlabs::ElevenLabs;
use tts::TTS;
use clipboard::Clipboard;

fn main() {
    // Initialize the ElevenLabs API client
    let api_key = "YOUR_API_KEY_HERE";
    let client = ElevenLabs::new(api_key);

    // Initialize the TTS client
    let tts = TTS::new();

    // Initialize the clipboard client
    let clipboard = Clipboard::new();

    // Get the contents of the clipboard
    let clipboard_text = clipboard.get_text().unwrap();

    // Use the ElevenLabs API to generate an audio file from the clipboard text
    let audio_file = client.generate_audio(clipboard_text).unwrap();

    // Use the TTS client to play the audio file
    tts.play_audio(audio_file).unwrap();
}
```
Replace `YOUR_API_KEY_HERE` with your actual ElevenLabs API key.

This code assumes that you have the `elevenlabs`, `tts`, and `clipboard` crates installed. If you don't have them installed, you can add them to your `Cargo.toml` file and run `cargo build` to install them.

Note that this is just a simple example, and you may want to add error handling and other features to your app.

Also, you will need to implement the `ElevenLabs` and `TTS` traits to use the `elevenlabs` and `tts` crates respectively. You can do this by creating a new file (e.g. `elevenlabs.rs`) and adding the following code:
```rust
// elevenlabs.rs
use reqwest;

pub struct ElevenLabs {
    api_key: String,
}

impl ElevenLabs {
    pub fn new(api_key: String) -> Self {
        ElevenLabs { api_key }
    }

    pub async fn generate_audio(&self, text: &str) -> Result<String, reqwest::Error> {
        let url = format!("https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/generate-audio?text={}&key={}", text, self.api_key);
        let response = reqwest::get(url).await?;
        let audio_file = response.text().await?;
        Ok(audio_file)
    }
}
```
